## Summary

I've found and analyzed the **no-intro loading screen** implementation in the NINEONELABS project. Here's the complete breakdown you requested:

---

## 1. NO-INTRO HTML MARKUP

**File**: `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/components/intro.php`

```html
<section id="intro" class="no-intro" aria-hidden="false">
    <div id="intro-card" class="no-intro__card">
        <div class="no-intro__metric">
            <span id="pct-text" class="no-intro__value">0</span>
            <span class="no-intro__suffix">%</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="c" class="no-intro__canvas"></canvas>
    </div>
</section>
```

**Key Elements & Classes**:
- Root: `<section id="intro" class="no-intro">` (fixed position overlay, hidden on load)
- Card container: `<div id="intro-card" class="no-intro__card">` (min 560px width, centered, black background)
- Percent display: `<span id="pct-text" class="no-intro__value">` (starts at 0, updates to 100)
- Canvas animation: `<canvas id="c" class="no-intro__canvas">` (where the progress bar is drawn)
- **Important**: Only included for `main` and `about` pages (line 393-395 of `main.php`)

---

## 2. SCSS STYLES

**File**: `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/components/_intro.scss`

```scss
@use "../abstract" as *;

.no-intro {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  z-index: var(--z-index-intro);
  width: 100%;
  height: 100vh;
  background: #000;
